    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106348" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδρᾰλέτ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέω</span>
		A) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>water-mill,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				12.3.30
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>engineer in charge of such a mill,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sardis
				7(1).169
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">iv/v A. D.</span>, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-αλέτα</span>):— <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδρόμυλοι</span>
			 also cites <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδρᾰλετ-αλετία</span></b> , ἡ, and in
				<u>Gloss.</u> we find <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδρᾰλετ-αλέσιον</span></b>  (prob. l.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
